; robosimstudio-base-task: cable_route/port_medium
; Single frozen sampler draw; run episode 0.
; Medium: four guides, 80 mm nominal pitch, half the original lateral stagger.
; The terminal is shifted 50 mm toward the robot. The start remains fixed.
; The 840 mm cable has 70 capsules and 71 scored points; require two points
; at each guide, three in the terminal region, and the free endpoint there.
; The rod was 720 mm at 60 capsules until the route was measured: it ate 607 mm
; median reaching the last station -- against 444 mm of straight lines between
; the seat points -- leaving a 99 mm tail for a nominal 113 mm port leg. At that
; length the scored portbox fraction sat at 0.049-0.066 against a 0.049 floor on
; every one of thirty trials, which is marginal on its face; at 840 mm it about
; doubles. 840 restores the reach at the SAME 12.00 mm capsule pitch and the same
; bend stiffness; the two fractions below moved only because the denominator did
; -- they are still two points and three points.
; Full graph cycle and settling precede evaluation.

(define (problem cablerouting-medium-routecable-81)

  (:suite cable_route)

  (:language weave the cable through the four pegs and route its free end into the port)

  (:staging
    (:cameras yam_station_cable@v1)
    ; THE BOARD IS DRAWN IN CENTIMETRES, THE TWO ENDS IN MILLIMETRES.
    ; `staging:PORT_BOARD` places all four pegs fresh every episode -- the gap between
    ; them, each one's stagger off the line, a wobble on top, the board's rotation
    ; and where it sits along the run -- inside the corridor its own two fittings
    ; leave, and draws the rod's shape beside them through the same four fractions
    ; `staging:CABLE_BOW` emits.
    ;
    ; Neither end is a constant either, and neither moves WITH the board. The
    ; anchor follows the cable, as it always did. The port is drawn in the 6 mm
    ; and 3 degrees of slop its own bolt slots leave -- enough that its mouth has
    ; to be found in the image every episode instead of remembered, far too little
    ; to make the reach into it a different task. The scored `portbox` rides the
    ; fixture, so the tolerance the route is judged at is unchanged.
    ;
    ; Every draw is measured against THIS board rather than against a band: the
    ; turning within a factor of two of its own 262.3 degrees and at its level, no
    ; crossing wrapped less than half as far as its weakest, seats disjoint, the
    ; hands not crowding, and the anchor-to-port run no longer than this one's
    ; plus 20 mm. A tier whose pegs were drawn into L3 at large would be a
    ; different experiment from the one its rates were calibrated on.
    ;
    ; The layout below is still what the scene builds when nothing samples, and
    ; it is what the sampler measures to find out what it is drawing beside.
    (:episodes (:count 1) (:seed 10080) (:sampler staging:PORT_BOARD_REACHABLE))
    ; RAISED FROM 12000 WITH THE WRAP. The crossing template now carries the
    ; span around each post instead of setting it down beside it, which costs
    ; ~304 control steps a station -- 1216 across this tier's four crossings. The
    ; ceiling was already binding: 6 of 18 pre-wrap Medium rows closed
    ; `truncated` rather than `policy_request`, so leaving it here would have
    ; scored the wrap on 90% of its own schedule and called the shortfall a
    ; worse route. This moves the BUDGET, not the goal -- every clause,
    ; tolerance, physics parameter and perception input is unchanged -- but
    ; rates either side of it are not comparable.
    ; RAISED AGAIN, from 13500. The first raise covered the wrap's own motion
    ; and still left the ceiling binding: 6 of 10 episodes closed `truncated`,
    ; and the one that seated ALL FOUR crossings was killed mid terminal carry
    ; -- `[plug] mouth refused at every height: BusClosed`, with the support
    ; hand already holding the free end. A truncated episode measures "did not
    ; fit in the budget", not "cannot do the task", so more than half the
    ; sample was saying nothing about the policy. Sized so the longest observed
    ; run finishes its carry, its restore pass and its verify with room over.
    ; THIRD RAISE, and the evidence for it is a completed route that scored 0.50.
    ; Episode 15 at the 18000 ceiling satisfied EVERY routing clause -- all four
    ; seats, cable in the port, free end in the port, goal.0 True throughout -- and
    ; failed only `goal.1.0`, the hand-clear check, with the TCP still 7.3 mm from
    ; the rod it had just placed against a 50 mm bar. The goal is worst_of(route,
    ; hand clear and settled), so a finished route scores 0.50 while the arm is
    ; still leaning on it. It was truncated mid-retreat, one motion short.
    ;
    ; 5 of 8 episodes closed `truncated` at 18000. Sized so the retreat and the
    ; settle that follow a completed route fit inside the budget rather than
    ; falling off the end of it. Slowness stays visible: cycle time is reported
    ; per successful episode, so a policy that needs every step of this says so.
    (:max-steps 24000)
    (:terminate-on-success false)
  )

  (:objects
    cable - port_medium_cable
  )

  (:fixtures
    peg0   - port_medium_peg0
    peg1   - port_medium_peg1
    peg2   - port_medium_peg2
    peg3   - port_medium_peg3
    anchor - port_medium_anchor
    port   - port_medium_port
  )

  (:regions
    (seat0    (:target peg0) (:ranges ((-0.045 -0.035 -0.003  0.035))))
    (seat1    (:target peg1) (:ranges (( 0.003 -0.035  0.045  0.035))))
    (seat2    (:target peg2) (:ranges ((-0.045 -0.035 -0.003  0.035))))
    (seat3    (:target peg3) (:ranges (( 0.003 -0.035  0.045  0.035))))
    (portbox  (:target port) (:ranges ((-0.045 -0.045  0.045 0.045))))
  )

  (:init)

  (:goal
    (worst_of
      (And
        (>= (containment cable seat0) 0.028169014085)
        (>= (containment cable seat1) 0.028169014085)
        (>= (containment cable seat2) 0.028169014085)
        (>= (containment cable seat3) 0.028169014085)
        (>= (containment cable portbox) 0.042253521127)
        (>= (containment cable.end_b portbox) 1.0)
      )
      (And
        (> (tcp-distance cable) 0.05)
        (<= (speed cable) 0.05)
      )
    )
  )

  (:reward (fraction))

  (:observe
    (once (<= (tcp-distance cable) 0.05))
    (straightness cable)
  )

  (:artifacts
    (:routine "routine:RoutineWeave")
    (:graph gt "graphs/weave")
    (:graph vision "graphs/weave")
  )

  (:provenance
    (:tier authored)
    (:source "AUTHORED -- no upstream. a four-station board at weave5's own pitch and depth with a terminal added at each end
              of the run, per VABAR Sec. V-A.6's Medium tier.")
    (:note "The reference cable scenes end at a peg line; a real run starts at something
            that holds it and finishes at something it is got into. The anchor is a
            bracket the rod is welded to (RodSpec.anchors), and the port is a goal
            clause rather than scenery.")
  )
)
